Changes in Version 0.18
  o Added the composite variable model family (experimental), following Schamberger, Schuberth, Henseler and Rosseel (2026, Behavior Research Methods):
    o cvm() estimates structural equation models with latent variables ('lambda') and composites ('weights'), related through 'beta' and covariances or a network ('latent')
    o cnm() is a wrapper for the composite network model (composite = "ggm"), which models a network of the indicators within every composite ('omega_c')
    o The new '_c' matrices (sigma_c, lowertri_c, kappa_c, omega_c and delta_c, rho_c and SD_c; argument 'composite') model the covariances of the indicators within composites
    o Variances and intercepts of composites are computed rather than estimated
    o A composite with a single indicator can be used to include an observed variable in the structural model
    o With latent = "ggm", a composite can either be part of the latent network or have incoming effects in 'beta', but not both
    o Composites are scaled by fixing the weight of the indicator with the largest starting weight to 1 (see the 'bad_marker_crit' argument)
    o sumscores = TRUE fixes all weights to 1, such that every composite is the sum score of its indicators
    o Supports multiple groups, the ML, FIML, ULS, WLS, DWLS, PML and PFIML estimators and the model search functions; ordinal data and correlation input are not yet supported
    o runmodel() warns when a composite is poorly scaled, reversed or not related to any other construct
    o prune() warns when it removes the last relation of a composite with the other constructs
  o fromlavaan() and tolavaan() now support models with composites (lavaan >= 0.7)
  o transmod() now supports the cvm family (e.g., transmod(x, composite = "ggm") turns a cvm model into a cnm model)
  o The notes on experimental features are shown again (once per session) until version 0.19, and now also for cvm() and cnm()
  o The warning of runmodel() on a large gradient now suggests identification = "variance" for lvm models
  o Fixed a bug in transmod() where transforming a diagonal structure added a free parameter
  o Fixed a bug in the R pipeline (usecpp(x, FALSE)) where derived SD matrices in getmatrix() had the wrong dimensions
  o Fixed a bug in the automatic penalty search (PML / PFIML with penalty_lambda = NA) where the first fit of the grid was not penalized

Changes in Version 0.17.7
  o Fixed a test that failed under the C collation locale (test suite only)

Changes in Version 0.17.6
  o Fixed test failures on CRAN check flavors with other BLAS/LAPACK builds: the tests now simulate data through a Cholesky factor instead of MASS::mvrnorm() (test suite only)
  o Updated a lavaan comparison test for lavaan >= 0.7

Changes in Version 0.17.5
  o The 'criterion' argument of ri_clpm_search() and ri_clpn_search() now defaults to "Chisq" instead of "BIC". Use criterion = "BIC" to recover old behavior

Changes in Version 0.17.4
  o Added a plot() method for psychonetrics models, which plots model matrices as networks using qgraph:
    o Default matrices are chosen per model family, and 'matrix' can be a vector to plot several matrices
    o Supports the 'group', 'time', 'threshold', 'alpha', 'adjust' and 'mode' arguments of getmatrix()
    o Covariance and precision matrices are standardized by default; use covariances = TRUE for the unstandardized matrix
    o Panels with the same nodes use the same layout (equalLayout = FALSE to disable) and are titled (titles = FALSE to disable)
  o Fixed a bug in the default 'matrices' of CIplot() for dlvm1 and ml_lvm models

Changes in Version 0.17.3
  o getmatrix() and CIplot() now support the matrix names of panelvar()/panelgvar() for ri_clpm() models (e.g., "beta", "PDC", "omega_zeta_within", "omega_zeta_between"), with a new 'time' argument to select the wave
  o Omitting 'time' returns one block per wave (waves constrained equal are collapsed); plain matrix names without 'time' still return the full matrix
  o CIplot() now plots the temporal, within-person and between-person blocks by default for ri_clpm() models

Changes in Version 0.17.2
  o Redesigned ri_clpm_search() as a decision tree:
    o If stationarity of the temporal effects is rejected, the search stops and the unconstrained model is selected
    o Rejected "contemporaneous", "intercepts" and "innovation" constraints are released and the search continues
    o The final panel(G)VAR step is only tested if the temporal, contemporaneous and innovation constraints are retained
    o Models that did not converge are never retained
    o Added the 'on_rejection' argument. Use on_rejection = "stop" to recover old behavior (stop at the first rejection)
    o The output now includes a 'verdicts' data frame with one row per step
  o Added ri_clpn() (ri_clpm() with type = "ggm") and the aliases ri_clpn_stationary() and ri_clpn_search()

Changes in Version 0.17.1
  o Added the 'stationary_means' argument to panelvar(), panelgvar() and dlvm1(). Use stationary_means = FALSE for wave-specific means (panelvar/panelgvar) or intercepts (dlvm1)
  o The baseline model now uses the same mean structure as the fitted model. Note: incremental fit indices are not comparable between models with stationary_means = TRUE and FALSE
  o panelvar(), panelgvar() and dlvm1() now give an informative error when 'means' is a character

Changes in Version 0.17.0
  o ri_clpm() now defaults to type = "cor" instead of "cov". Use type = "cov" to recover old behavior
  o ri_clpm_search() now adds constraints in the order: temporal effects, contemporaneous relations, intercepts, innovation variances, panel(G)VAR

Changes in Version 0.16.9
  o Tests with ordinal data are now skipped when the 'pbv' package cannot be used (test suite only)

Changes in Version 0.16.8
  o The method used for the saturated log-likelihood is now stored in x@baseline_saturated$satMethodUsed, and the new fit measure 'satLL_analytic' indicates if the analytic formula was used (GitHub issue #53)
  o saturated = "model" no longer falls back to the analytic saturated log-likelihood; only saturated = "default" does
  o Fixed stepup() failing with ordinal data (GitHub issue #54):
    o freepar() now uses small starting values when EPC-based starting values are improper
    o runmodel() now retries with emergency starting values when the optimizer stalls at improper values
    o stepup() now handles a missing chi-square difference test or criterion

Changes in Version 0.16.7
  o Added dlvm(), tsdlvm(), meta_var(), ml_var() and ml_gvar() as primary names for dlvm1(), tsdlvm1(), meta_var1(), ml_var1() and ml_gvar1(); the old names remain supported
  o 'within' and 'between' are now the preferred argument names in panelvar() and ml_var(); the *_latent names remain supported
  o ml_var() and ml_gvar() now default to estimator = "auto": FIML (through panelvar) with at most 10 occasions per subject, and the two-level pseudo-ML estimator otherwise
  o ml_var1() and ml_gvar1() now support estimator = "FIML"
  o Added a summary() method for psychonetrics models
  o Added (experimental) ml_varcov() and the wrappers ml_ggm() and ml_corr() for multi-level variance-covariance models; supports the "ML" and "FIML" estimators
  o meta_var1() and meta_gvar() now give an informative error with more than 11 variables, and a warning when the number of studies is small
  o Fixed ml_lvm() failing or permuting observations when the data were not sorted by cluster
  o Fixed samplestats() crashing when some pairwise covariances could not be computed
  o Fixes for R-devel in examples and tests

Changes in Version 0.16.6
  o Added (experimental) ml_var1() and the wrapper ml_gvar1(): multi-level VAR(1) and graphical VAR models for intensive longitudinal data, using a two-level pseudo-ML estimator

Changes in Version 0.16.5
  o Added sampling weights via the 'sampling_weights' argument of varcov() and lvm(), with robust standard errors and a scaled test statistic (complete continuous data only)
  o Documented that residual covariances among endogenous latent variables are not freed by default (unlike lavaan)
  o Fixed fromlavaan() for single-group lavaan models without a mean structure
  o Fixed the baseline and saturated models of fixed_x models, which are now conditioned on the exogenous variables (CFI and TLI were incorrect)
  o Fixed the scaled chi-square difference test in compare() for the MLMV, MLMVS and WLSMV estimators
  o Faster model construction and robust ML estimation for models with many variables

Changes in Version 0.16.4
  o Added the PDC (partial directed correlation) parameterization of temporal effects: temporal = "PDC" in var1()/gvar(), panelvar()/panelgvar() and tsdlvm1(), and temporal_latent = "PDC" and temporal_residual = "PDC" in dlvm1()
    o The PDC matrix encodes from = row and to = column
    o CIplot(), the model search functions and penalized estimation use the PDC matrix by default for these models
  o checkFisher() is now exact for FIML models

Changes in Version 0.16.3
  o Added the 'beta_epsilon' argument to dlvm1() for lag-1 temporal effects between residuals ("zero" by default; "diag", "full" or a matrix)
  o getmatrix(x, "sigma_epsilon_within_stationary") returns the implied stationary residual covariances
  o A non-zero beta_epsilon requires at least three waves

Changes in Version 0.16.2
  o panelvar() and panelgvar() are now implemented as their own model framework instead of through dlvm1(), which is faster and gives the same results
  o The means of panelvar/panelgvar models are now in the 'mu' matrix (previously 'nu'), and variable names default to the rownames of the design matrix

Changes in Version 0.16.1
  o Added type = "cor" (correlations 'rho' and standard deviations 'SD') to all typed covariance structures in lvm(), var1(), tsdlvm1(), dlvm1(), ml_lvm(), meta_lvm(), meta_var1(), ri_clpm() and their wrappers
  o With identification = "variance" the latent standard deviations are fixed to 1 for type = "cor"

Changes in Version 0.16
  o Version 0.16 consolidates the 0.15.x versions. The most important additions are:
    o A fast two-level ML estimator for ml_lvm()
    o The robust ML estimators MLM, MLMV, MLMVS and MLR, with scaled chi-square difference tests in compare()
    o fromlavaan() and tolavaan() to convert models from and to lavaan
    o Standardized solutions, the wishart likelihood and fixed exogenous covariates (fixed_x)
    o A large number of bug fixes and an automated test suite

Changes in Version 0.15.31
  o Added a two-level ML estimator to ml_lvm() (estimator = "ML"), which is much faster than FIML for large clusters. The 'estimator' argument now defaults to "default"; use estimator = "FIML" to recover old behavior
  o Added the robust ML estimators "MLM", "MLMV", "MLMVS" and "MLR" (robust standard errors, scaled test statistics and robust fit indices)
  o compare() now reports a scaled chi-square difference test for robust estimators (see the 'scaled.test.method' argument)
  o Added fromlavaan() and tolavaan() to convert lvm models from and to lavaan
  o parameters(x, standardized = TRUE) now returns the standardized solution with standard errors for the lvm and varcov families
  o Added likelihood = "wishart" to lvm() and varcov()
  o Added the 'fixed_x' argument to lvm() and varcov() for fixed exogenous covariates
  o Fixed the scaled test statistic of multi-group models with equality constraints

Changes in Version 0.15.30
  o Fixed the penalty for improper (non-positive definite) implied covariance matrices, which could make the optimizer diverge in panel and SEM models
  o Fixed the "LBFGS++" optimizer reporting convergence at infeasible points
  o Fixed emergencystart() constraining the wrong edges to zero
  o latentgrowth() now uses least-squares starting values for the latent means
  o Fixed elastic-net penalized ML applying the ridge penalty twice (LASSO was not affected)
  o Fixed a bug in the spectral shift used for starting values; starting values of dlvm1 models may change slightly
  o Fixed fullFIML = TRUE giving an error
  o Fixed equal = "omega_zeta" being ignored in lvm models
  o Fixed factorscores() for models with regressions and latent means
  o Fixed varcov(covtype = "choose") not rescaling unbiased covariances
  o Fixed the p-value adjustment in prune() for parameters with equality constraints
  o Fixed prune(recursive = TRUE) resetting 'alpha' and other arguments after the first step
  o Fixed the ebic.75 fit measure; likelihood-based fit measures are now also returned without a baseline model
  o Fixed getmatrix(..., diag = FALSE) setting the wrong elements to zero
  o Fixed runmodel(analyticFisher = FALSE) not using the numeric Fisher information
  o Standard errors are now NA (with a warning) when the estimated variance is negative
  o Fixed setestimator(), parequal() and lvm models with latent = "ggm" and a single latent variable
  o fixpar() and related functions now give an error for unknown variable labels
  o Ising and Blume-Capel models: improved numerical stability, data are now checked against 'responses', and only missing = "listwise" is supported
  o Fixed groupequal("delta") in Blume-Capel models
  o Fixed the 'sigma_within' matrix returned for dlvm1 models (estimation was not affected)
  o Fixed the stationarity constraints of ri_clpm models after pruning
  o Fixed tsData() ignoring 'lags', 'scale', 'center' and 'centerWithin' for grouped data
  o Added the 'centerWithin' argument to var1() and gvar()
  o Fixed variable names with special characters being dropped in ml_lvm, dlvm1 and ri_clpm
  o meta_varcov() now supports covariance matrices as input
  o Added the "OS_individual" and "OS_pooled" options for 'Vmethod' in meta_varcov()
  o Fixed several crashes in meta_varcov(), meta_ggm() and meta_lvm()
  o The 'matrices' argument of addMIs() is now implemented
  o loop_psychonetrics() and replicator() gain a 'seed' argument
  o aggregate_bootstraps() now respects the 'remove_problematic' argument
  o Removed the "MUML" option from ml_lvm(), which was not implemented
  o Faster modification indices in multi-group models, model construction and Ising models
  o Added an automated test suite (tinytest) and removed the unused dependencies GA, combinat, VCA and abind
  o Large documentation cleanup

