Changes in Version 0.15
  o Version 0.15 consolidates the 0.14.x versions. The most important changes are:
    o Faster estimation through optimized C++ code, and the new "LBFGS++" optimizer
    o Ordinal data support and WLSMV estimation in lvm()
    o dlvm1() now accepts wide-format and long-format data; ml_tsdlvm1(), ml_gvar(), ml_var() and related wrappers are deprecated
    o Penalized ML (PML) and penalized FIML (PFIML) estimation with automatic selection of the penalty, and refit()
    o Added meta_lvm(), meta_var1() and meta_gvar()
    o Added write_psychonetrics() and loop_psychonetrics()
    o Added the 'cors', 'groupvar' and 'corinput' arguments to all model families
    o Added the SRMR fit measure
    o Missing data handling now defaults to missing = "auto" (FIML when data are missing)
    o Approximate standard errors are used when the Fisher information matrix cannot be inverted
    o lvm() now accepts lambda = "full"
    o penalize() now accepts a matrix for the 'lambda' argument
    o Improved starting values for 'beta' and various bug fixes

Changes in Version 0.14.28
  o Ising models now compute model-implied means and covariances, which enables the SRMR fit measure

Changes in Version 0.14.27
  o Removed the roptim-based C++ optimizers (cpp_L-BFGS-B, cpp_BFGS, cpp_CG, cpp_SANN, cpp_Nelder-Mead). Use "nlminb" (default), "ucminf", "nloptr_TNEWTON" or "LBFGS++" instead
  o Added the SRMR fit measure
  o The 'beta_min' argument of find_penalized_lambda() and runmodel() now accepts "numerical" (default), "theoretical" or a numeric value
  o Added a C++ implementation of meta_var1/meta_gvar models
  o Fixed the starting values of delta matrices when using delta_* = "zero"
  o Replaced deprecated ggplot2::aes_string() calls

Changes in Version 0.14.26
